{"name":"Battleship Grey","hex":"#6f7476","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"battleship grey","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A medium grey color tinged with blue, like that of a battleship."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a medium grey color tinged with blue, like that of a battleship."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/battleship_grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Battleship Grey","blocks":[{"text":"\"Battleship Grey\" is a song by Dutch DJ and producer DJ Tiësto featuring vocals from English singer Kirsty Hawkshaw, recorded in 2000. It is included on Tiësto's first album, In My Memory, and on Hawkshaw's album, Meta Message."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f0/DJ_Ti%C3%ABsto_feat._Kirsty_Hawkshaw_-_Battleship_Grey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battleship_Grey","wikidata":"Q4873231"},{"title":"Shades of gray","blocks":[{"text":"Variations of gray or grey include achromatic grayscale shades, which lie exactly between white and black, and nearby colors with low colorfulness. A selection of a number of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Shades_of_Gray.svg/330px-Shades_of_Gray.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_gray","wikidata":"Q3958716"},{"title":"Battleship","blocks":[{"text":"A battleship was a heavily armored large warship with a main battery consisting of large guns, designed to serve as a capital ship. From their advent in the late 1880s, battleships were among the largest and most formidable warship types ever built, until they were surpassed by aircraft carriers beginning in the 1940s. The modern battleship traces its origin to the sailing ship of the line, which was developed into the steam ship of the line and soon thereafter the ironclad warship. After a period of extensive experimentation in the 1870s and 1880s, ironclad design was largely standardized by the British Royal Sovereign class, which are usually referred to as the first \"pre-dreadnought battleships\". These ships carried an armament that usually included four large guns and several medium-caliber guns that were to be used against enemy battleships, and numerous small guns for self defense."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/BB61_USS_Iowa_BB61_broadside_USN.jpg/330px-BB61_USS_Iowa_BB61_broadside_USN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battleship","wikidata":"Q182531"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/SilverB.JPG/500px-SilverB.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/SilverB.JPG/1280px-SilverB.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/SilverB.JPG/500px-SilverB.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilverB.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Campfire_scar_08319.JPG/500px-Campfire_scar_08319.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 